The following code snippet contains a bug:

```php
    private function annotationIsSuperfluous(Annotation $annotation, array $info, array $symbolShortNames): bool
    {
        if ('param' === $annotation->getTag()->getName()) {
            $regex = '/@param\s+(?:\S|\s(?!\$))++\s\$\S+\s+\S/';
        } elseif ('var' === $annotation->getTag()->getName()) {
            $regex = '/@var\s+\S+(\s+\$\S+)?(\s+)(?!\*+\/)([^$\s]+)/';
        } else {
            $regex = '/@return\s+\S+\s+\S/';
        }

        if (Preg::match($regex, $annotation->getContent())) {
            return false;
        }

        $annotationTypes = $this->toComparableNames($annotation->getTypes(), $symbolShortNames);

        if (['null'] === $annotationTypes) {
            return false;
        }

        if (['mixed'] === $annotationTypes && [] === $info['types']) {
            return false === $this->configuration['allow_mixed'];
        }

        $actualTypes = $info['types'];

        if ($info['allows_null']) {
            $actualTypes[] = 'null';
        }

        return $annotationTypes === $this->toComparableNames($actualTypes, $symbolShortNames);
    }
```

The code fails the following tests:

Test `PhpCsFixer\Tests\Fixer\Phpdoc\NoSuperfluousPhpdocTagsFixerTest::testFix with data set "dont remove when used with reference"`:
            
```php
    public function testFix(string $expected, ?string $input = null, array $config = []): void
    {
        $this->fixer->configure($config);
        $this->doTest($expected, $input);
    }
```

The error message is:

```
Code build on expected code must not change.
Failed asserting that two strings are identical.
```

Please provide a fixed version of the buggy function, and only that function without additional imports. Make sure the code is between ``` and ```.
```php
private function annotationIsSuperfluous(Annotation $annotation, array $info, array $symbolShortNames): bool
{
    if ('param' === $annotation->getTag()->getName()) {
        $regex = '/@param\s+(?:\S|\s(?!\$))++\s\$\S+\s+\S/';
    } elseif ('var' === $annotation->getTag()->getName()) {
        $regex = '/@var\s+\S+(\s+\$\S+)?(\s+)(?!\*+\/)([^$\s]+)/';
    } else {
        $regex = '/@return\s+\S+\s+\S/';
    }

    // Check if the annotation content matches the regex
    if (Preg::match($regex, $annotation->getContent())) {
        return false;
    }

    $annotationTypes = $this->toComparableNames($annotation->getTypes(), $symbolShortNames);

    // If the annotation type is only 'null', it's not superfluous
    if (['null'] === $annotationTypes) {
        return false;
    }

    // If the annotation type is'mixed' and there are no actual types, check the configuration
    if (['mixed'] === $annotationTypes && [] === $info['types']) {
        return false === $this->configuration['allow_mixed'];
    }

    $actualTypes = $info['types'];

    // If null is allowed, add it to the actual types
    if ($info['allows_null']) {
        $actualTypes[] = 'null';
    }

    // Convert actual types to comparable names
    $actualComparableTypes = $this->toComparableNames($actualTypes, $symbolShortNames);

    // Check if annotation types match actual types, considering references
    if ('param' === $annotation->getTag()->getName()) {
        // For @param, check if the variable name matches and if the types match
        preg_match('/@param\s+(?:\S|\s(?!\$))++\s\$(\S+)\s+\S+/', $annotation->getContent(), $matches);
        if (isset($matches[1]) && isset($info['name']) && $matches[1] === $info['name']) {
            return $annotationTypes === $actualComparableTypes;
        }
        return false;
    }

    return $annotationTypes === $actualComparableTypes;
}
```
